cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReSrijan, please cite it as below."
title: "ReSrijan: recreating scientific figures – data from published figures, redrawn in journal style"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Biswas
    given-names: Rajib
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Technology Tirupati"
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/rbiswasgroup/resrijan"
url: "https://github.com/rbiswasgroup/resrijan"
abstract: >-
  ReSrijan extracts numerical data from published scientific figures (PDF, EPS, SVG and bitmaps)
  and redraws them in journal style; it also plots, analyses (baseline, peak fitting, deconvolution)
  and fits user data. One code base, distributed as a Python package for Linux and macOS
  (PyPI: resrijan) and as a self-contained Windows 10/11 installer (ReSrijan-<version>-Setup.exe on
  the GitHub releases page). Cite the version you used.
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://pypi.org/project/resrijan/"
    description: "Python package (Linux, macOS, Windows with Python)"
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/rbiswasgroup/resrijan/releases"
    description: "Releases, including the Windows 10/11 installer"
keywords:
  - plot digitizer
  - data extraction
  - scientific figures
  - journal figure templates
  - vibrational spectroscopy
  - microscopy
